subproblems.statement:
Let P ∈ ℕ, O ⊆ ℝ^P open, K ⊆ O compact, and f : ℝ^P → ℝ^P of class C¹ on O (ContDiffOn ℝ 1 f O; f is arbitrary off O). Then there exist:
- a map φ : ℝ^P → ℝ^P of class C¹ on all of ℝ^P (ContDiff ℝ 1 φ);
- an open set V ⊆ ℝ^P with K ⊆ V;
- a compact set K' with K' ⊆ O;
such that φ(x) = f(x) and Dφ(x) = Df(x) for every x ∈ V (Df(x) := fderiv ℝ f x), and φ(x) = x for every x ∉ K'.

Setting:
- P, n ∈ ℕ and U ⊆ ℝ^P open;
- R = (M, θ, ξ) an integer multiplicity triple in U (IMRep U n) representing T ∈ 𝒟_n(U);
- K ⊆ U compact, and φ : ℝ^P → ℝ^P of class C¹ on ℝ^P (ContDiff ℝ 1 φ) with φ(x) = x for every x ∉ K;
- S ∈ 𝒟_n(U) with S(ω) = ∫_M θ(x)·ξ(x)(ω(φ(x))∘Dφ(x)) dHⁿ(x) for every ω ∈ 𝒟ⁿ(U), where Dφ(x) = fderiv ℝ φ x, Hⁿ = μHE[n] and β∘L := β.compContinuousLinearMap L.
Claim: if ∂T = 0 in U (BoundaryVanishes T; vacuous for n = 0), then ∂S = 0 in U (BoundaryVanishes S).
